ey're  going to have unbelievable future well I  didn't stop being Leia I mean it doesn't  go away it's like a persistent rash no  no but I  I am print I had stayed in character for  the last 35 years I count it from the  last movie but if we count it from the  first it's 40 years  but people identify me with her so much  and I am the custodian of Princess Leia  so I try to keep her fit and ready for  action I were general outfits I know I  haven't changed it because I'm general  because they didn't tell me I was  general until it was too late and then I  was suddenly general and what I have  said though is in terms of being general  or princess even though Princess is kind  of Nellie and it it's something that you  inherit and so it's general is something  that generally you have to rise through  the ranks and so forth  Princess Leia theoretically a princess  would get better clothes not good  hairstyles but better clothes and even  then but still general clothing you've  seen them and those hats if I think that  my hair was bad imagine wearing one of  those iron has she's very focused very  disciplined very passionate committed to  what she does and I have those qualities  but not choose don't laugh at me I do  have those qualities but not I don't  have control over them and I don't have  them as intensely and she's very  organized and I would say maybe I'm not  organized  because she was really the first female  character that and it's not it they're  not the characters in Star Wars are very  human they're not superpower  I mean yes we have the force but you  know if you are very good and you work  very hard Santa will bring you the force  for Christmas no but it doesn't seem  that out of reach you know their  characters you can identify with and  their characters where you feel like  well if they can do that you know I  could do that so you know that she can  do what she can do and she can also do  what she can't do well it was just  amazing to be there I'm older now and I  could pay attention because when you're  young and you're doing those things  you're just moving through your life  like you know you'll be able to reflect  on it they don't tell you that you lose  your memory and that your ability to  reflect is impacted by memory loss  severely so I can pay attention this  time and I can also watch these younger  people you know experience it and and I  wonder if it was like that for me and I  suspect it was you know so that's I  could retrieve my memory through them  and also my daughter is a little part in  it so that was fun to have my daughter  around  I think they'll love it they go and they  go in to love it so what if you think  can happen with something like that  you're you're gonna be disappointed no  matter what you know because you're  going in thinking it'll be some  life-changing experience but if you go  into the movie just to you know  reacquaint yourself with some old  friends and get into these situations  that we're incredibly exciting and now  familiar they'll just have a really good  time I think because it'll be  reminiscent and because it's new and we  have some new folks and I think they'll  love it  JJ's awesome he is incredible infectious  enthusiasm he's a huge fan of Star Wars  and which was I think daunting for him  because he grew up watching the movies  as well so how are you gonna so he had  that kind of pressure but you never saw  that and he's very confident and he  learned everyone's name I'm not kidding  even my dog's name but then my dog is  very famous he just just he has high  verbal acuity which I appreciate  enormously he's fun to listen to and  even though he's younger than I am by  like an hour that feels more like 10  years he has a lot of the same sort of  media references he he knows movies he  knows music you know and he loves his  job so it's a pleasure to watch anybody  enjoy what they're doing when did it hit  you that you were actually directing  this movie what was t